{"ID": 624022558337007616, "Timestamp": "2019-09-18 23:22:51", "Contents": "Impact A:  According to the worldbank (org) if the BRI is completed, transport projects could reduce travel times along economic corridors by 12%. This is significant, because estimates suggest that if all other drivers of growth were to increase by 10% and transport infrastructure was to stay constant, then growth in income would be just 9%. As a result of economic growth and trade, 7.6 million people will be lifted from extreme poverty. 1 billion children worldwide are living in poverty. According to UNICEF, 22,000 children die each day due to poverty. (https://www.dosomething.org/us/facts/11-facts-about-global-poverty)", "Attachments": ""},
